Hermit kernel (hermit-rs tag hermit-0.13.0, kernel ef27b79): seed the
kernel's entropy pool from the Armv8.5 RNG on aarch64.

Upstream, `seed_entropy()` on aarch64 always returns `None`, so
`sys_read_entropy` falls back to a 31-bit Park-Miller generator and still
reports success. Rust std seeds every thread's HashMap from it, so those
seeds are predictable (spec 20, *Entropy*). With this patch the pool is
seeded from RNDRSS when the CPU has FEAT_RNG; without it nothing changes.
Chitala's own randomness never comes from the kernel either way.

Upstream merged an equivalent fix on 2026-07-26 (hermit-os/kernel#2528,
RNDR seeding), after the hermit-0.13.2 release, so no release contains it
yet. native/run.sh applies this patch to a copy of the pinned kernel; drop
it when the pin moves to a release with #2528.

--- a/src/arch/aarch64/kernel/processor.rs
+++ b/src/arch/aarch64/kernel/processor.rs
@@ -195,8 +195,31 @@
 	}
 }
 
+/// Reads a seed from the Armv8.5 random number generator (FEAT_RNG).
+///
+/// Returns `None` if the CPU has no RNG or it keeps reporting failures.
 pub fn seed_entropy() -> Option<[u8; 32]> {
-	None
+	// A failing read sets the Z flag; retry a bounded number of times so that a
+	// broken RNG makes entropy unavailable instead of hanging the kernel.
+	const RETRIES: usize = 1024;
+
+	let rng = aarch64_cpu::asm::random::ArmRng::new()?;
+	let mut buf = [0; 32];
+
+	for word in buf.chunks_mut(8) {
+		// RNDRSS reseeds from the true entropy source before returning, which is
+		// what a seed for the kernel's ChaCha20 generator should come from.
+		let value = (0..RETRIES).find_map(|_| {
+			let value = rng.rndrss();
+			if value.is_none() {
+				core::hint::spin_loop();
+			}
+			value
+		})?;
+		word.copy_from_slice(&value.to_ne_bytes());
+	}
+
+	Some(buf)
 }
 
